But...

As a scientist well-trained in biology and chemistry, all my instincts
rebel against such an idea on the grounds that it goes directly
contrary to the general trend in our (and, presumably, the Nethack)
universe...which is, of course, entropy.

Over time, stuff should get duller, blunter, more rotted, less shiny --
not better. Weapons should lose their edge, suits of armour fall apart,
food crumble and rot, potions partially evaporate. Scrolls and
spellbooks should fade, metal bands of rings erode, keys and lanterns
break, gems get duller.

Not saying I like it, but that's the way the world works. Otherwise,
*I* could just sit in a corner and contemplate my navel, and, just by
virtue of the fact that time is passing, make a billion dollars, obtain
a stunning physique, and become ruler of the world. ;-)

